  "interpretation": {
    "vrf": "Four-row block-scale allocation is [512,8192) per slice in both images. Activation scale is [0,32) in whole and [32,64) in probe. Tail allocations also fit. No live address collision or premature register/table use was found. This does not establish all encoded indexer or runtime behavior.",
    "lookup_supply_difference": "Whole prepares all eight native lookup tables before the first native stream (last StoTab end84867, first native begin87025). Probe overlaps the first four native streams with later StoTab commands. Its first native interval76017..78680 also overlaps three lookup-source DmaLoad intervals75902..76740,76740..77578,77578..78416. This identifies a changed concurrency window, not a measured stall.",
    "bank_hypothesis": "Concurrent Main lookup execution, Sub table preparation and DMA are a conditional SRAM-bank/resource-contention hypothesis. Graph/schedule and launch-code4 provide no observed bank-access run, reset reason, stalled instruction, or failure timestamp. No one bank-conflict condition or causal timeout source is established. Whole also has concurrent DMA during native execution, so DMA overlap alone does not discriminate the failure.",
    "separate_results": "Whole v2 standard-input correctness and measured regression are distinct from the standalone probe launch failure. The timeout neither demonstrates whole-kernel output mismatch nor a general SDK inability to perform fused native arithmetic. V1 probe success cannot replace V2 probe validation."
  },
  "documentation_sentence": "E131 v2 whole FFN passed its standard correctness screen but regressed in measured cycles. Its separate boundary-probe image timed out on the first case before producing output comparisons. Static comparison found a different lookup-table preparation overlap, with no VRF overflow or live table alias found; the timeout cause remains unresolved.",
  "limits": [
    "The schedule is a compiler estimate, not an internal NPU trace.",
    "No access timing, bank IDs, same-bank cumulative count or firmware fault location is present in the raw failure log.",
    "No repair or further tile experiment is proposed by this audit. Adoption/tuning closure is recorded separately."
  ]
}
